      "writtenOn": "2017-11-15T16:47:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can\u0027t redefine the 32-bit version as 64 bits, unless existing EC implementations guarantee the top 32 bits were 0.\n\nIf current implementations can have non-zero top 32 bits, won\u0027t that cause the host to process spurious events on older systems?\n\nInstead, I think we need to define EC_MKBP_EVENT_HOST_EVENT64 \u003d 7, indicating the top 32 bits are populated.",
